-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the σ_z-weighted closing: the quantum triad
-- tr(σ_k M_e) = tr(σ_k h_e √V h_e⁻¹): σ_k inserted between the line's two indices at v. In the Bargmann realization the
-- line's index at v is the open variable w (degree 1), on which 2J_z = 2(w∂_w − ½) is diagonal: −1 on monomials without
-- w and +1 on those with w. So the σ_z-weighted closing is R after that sign. Its image is no longer invariant: it is the
-- weight-zero component of a spin-1 vector of the vertex, kept here over the vertex's weight-zero monomials.
sigma-entry : (List Nat → List Nat → SQ) → List Nat → List Nat → SQ
sigma-entry rent t s = sq-mul (if eqb (exp-last s) zero then sq-neg sq-one else sq-one) (rent t s)
